"use strict";(globalThis.webpackChunk_8x8_developer_docs=globalThis.webpackChunk_8x8_developer_docs||[]).push([[86240],{94390:e=>{e.exports=JSON.parse('{"id":"2026-10-27-sms-inbound-mms-media-urls","date":"2026-10-27","products":["Connect","APIs"],"product":"Connect","channel":"SMS","changeType":"Added","title":"Inbound MMS media on the inbound SMS webhook","excerpt":"When a user sends an MMS to one of your MMS-enabled US/Canada virtual numbers, the inbound SMS webhook (inboundmessagereceived) now includes a mediaUrls array with a link to each media file, alongside the message text in body. mediaUrls is omitted for plain SMS.","hasArticle":true,"bodyHtml":"<p>When a user sends an MMS to one of your MMS-enabled US/Canada virtual numbers, the inbound SMS webhook (<code>inbound_message_received</code>) now includes a <code>mediaUrls</code> array with a link to each media file, alongside the message text in <code>body</code>. <code>mediaUrls</code> is omitted for plain SMS.</p>\\n<p>The links are not the carrier&#39;s own URLs: 8x8 copies each media file into its own storage and sends you a pre-signed URL that is valid for 1 day by default. Download the media when the webhook arrives if you need to keep it. If a media file cannot be copied, the message is still delivered with its text and the remaining media.</p>\\n<p>Media is only included in the latest inbound SMS format. If your webhook receives a different structure, contact support to activate the latest format for your account.</p>\\n<p>Delivery receipts for MMS you send use the same <code>outbound_message_status_changed</code> webhook as SMS. Only the <code>queued</code> receipt sent when the message is accepted carries the <code>outboundContent</code> object with the <code>mediaUrls</code> that were sent; later receipts report the delivery status only.</p>\\n<h2>Read more</h2>\\n<ul>\\n<li><a href=\\"/connect/docs/inbound-sms\\">Inbound SMS</a></li>\\n<li><a href=\\"/connect/docs/delivery-receipts-for-outbound-sms\\">Delivery receipts for outbound SMS</a></li>\\n<li><a href=\\"/connect/docs/send-sms-api-reference\\">Send SMS API</a></li>\\n</ul>\\n"}')}}]);